The device's POPS folder has old BDMA drivers -- copy this release's POPS folder there.
Los archivos del juego y de la VMC usan %d/%d fragmentos, superando el límite compartido de Neutrino. ¿Omitir la VMC %s y usar la tarjeta de memoria física en la ranura %d?
Rebuild
Copies this card into one unbroken file the native core can use. Needs free space for one copy while it runs.
Too fragmented for the native core
Rebuild this VMC? Its saves are copied into a new file in one piece and checked byte by byte before it replaces the card. No backup file is made.
VMC rebuilt in one piece.
Not enough unbroken free space to rebuild this VMC. Nothing was changed. Free up space on the device and try again.
The VMC could not be rebuilt. Nothing was changed.
Rebuild cancelled. Nothing was changed.
The VMC was copied but could not be swapped in. Your saves are in the .new file in the VMC folder -- if the card does not come back, rename that file to .bin on a PC.
The VMC was rebuilt, but the HDD could not confirm the change was saved. Check the card's saves before relying on it.
