Alternate Background
Shows the theme's alternate background (alt= in its conf_theme.cfg) instead of its default one. Themes without one are not changed.
Series card: the games in this series use this name by default, so saves on it can carry over between them.
Game card: named after this game's ID.
Generic card: shared by every game set to the same generic card.
This Neutrino has no SMB support -- launching with the OPL core.
Neutrino reaches SMB on port 445 only -- launching with the OPL core.
This server does not offer SMB 3.0, which Neutrino needs -- launching with the OPL core.
Neutrino cannot write a VMC on the SMB share -- launching with the OPL core.
These SMB settings are beyond Neutrino's limits -- launching with the OPL core.
The game list changed while this was open, so nothing was done. Please try again.
Boot Theme Wait
Seconds the start-up screen waits for your saved theme while its drive starts up. 0 = Off: the menu opens right away and your theme appears as soon as it is found.
PS1 Duplicates
A PS1 game that is both a POPSTARTER VCD and an Ember image. Both: two rows. Ember: the Ember one only. POPSTARTER: the VCD only. The same title, ignoring case and a leading disc ID, is the same game. Display only.
Both
List Title and Description
The Title and Description from a game's CFG that a theme shows beside the game list. Theme: as the theme sets them. On: shown even if the theme turns them off. Off: hidden. The info page shows them either way.
App Handoff Path
Legacy: BDM apps receive massN:/...; other devices keep their normal launch paths. Typed: supported BDM apps receive usbN:/..., ataN:/..., ilinkN:/... or mx4sioN:/... when identified, otherwise massN:. Only the path passed to the app changes; ELF loading is unchanged. Per-app cfg: HANDOFFPATH=LEGACY or TYPED.
Legacy (mass)
Typed (usb0:, ata0:)
Console i.LINK ID
Native OPL core only; Neutrino ignores it. Enter 16 hexadecimal digits in byte order. Empty or all zeros uses this console's ID. This does not change i.LINK storage hardware.
Console i.LINK ID must be empty or exactly 16 hexadecimal digits (0-9, A-F). Settings were not saved.
The stored Console i.LINK ID is invalid and was ignored. This game will use the real console ID.
%d: The SMB2 driver did not load. Browsing with SMBv1 instead until the next start.
